ing Streamlit. I'm asked to act as a product manager and provide analysis, then say \\\"\u8bf7\u5de5\u7a0b\u5e08\u5f00\u59cb\u5b9e\u73b0\\\". This is a simulated multi-agent setup. Let me provide a structured PM analysis: requirements understanding, module division, tech selection, priority, acceptance criteria. Be concise but complete.\\n\\nLet me think about details:\\n\\nRequirements:\\n- Real-time BTC price in USD\\n- 24h change (percent and absolute)\\n- Refresh functionality\\n\\nTech: Streamlit, API source (CoinGecko free API /simple/price, or Binance API, or Coinbase). Recommend CoinGecko as primary with fallback to Binance/Coinbase.\\n\\nData fields: current price, 24h change %, 24h change absolute, 24h high/low optional, last updated time, data source.\\n\\nError handling: network timeout, rate limiting (429), malformed JSON, missing fields, empty response.\\n\\nLoading state: st.spinner, skeleton.\\n\\nCaching: st.cache_data with ttl=10 or so \u2014 but refresh button needs to bypass cache. Use cache ttl short and a refresh button that clears cache (st.cache_data.clear() or use a nonce).\\n\\nState: use st.session_state to store last data so on error we can show last known price with a warning.\\n\\nUI: metric components, colored delta (st.metric handles automatically with delta, but Streamlit's metric delta color: positive green, negative red \u2014 default is inverse for some; can use delta_color=\\\"normal\\\").\\n\\nAuto-refresh optional \u2014 st.autorefresh or use st_autorefresh from streamlit-extras. Keep it optional; maybe a checkbox. Actually \\\"\u5b9e\u65f6\\\" \u2014 could add optional auto-refresh toggle. But keep scope: manual refresh required; auto-refresh as optional enhancement (P1).\\n\\nPriority:\\nP0: fetch data + display price + 24h change + refresh + error handling\\nP1: last updated time, data source label, auto-refresh toggle, fallback API\\nP2: chart of 7d price, multiple currencies, dark mode styling\\n\\nAcceptance criteria: concrete testable items.\\n\\nThen say \\\"\u8bf7\u5de5\u7a0b\u5e08\u5f00\u59cb\u5b9e\u73b0\\\".\\n\\nKeep it reasonably concise but complete. Use markdown structure.\",\"type\":\"ThoughtEvent\"}]},\"name\":\"ProductManager\"}", "sender": "ProductManager_5bbb1907-a4dd-4176-ad5e-8195a7b33495/5bbb1907-a4dd-4176-ad5e-8195a7b33495", "receiver": null, "kind": "MessageKind.PUBLISH", "delivery_stage": "DeliveryStage.DELIVER", "type": "Message"}
